body:
It doesn't seem like the body of `_get_property_list` has much effect, even this is enough to crash the editor:

```cpp
void ComputeShaderTask::_get_property_list(List<PropertyInfo>* p_list) const {
	ERR_FAIL_NULL(p_list);
	PropertyInfo p(Variant::Type::FLOAT, "my_property");
	p_list->push_back(p);
}
```

It seems like any call to `p_list->push_back` here will result in a crash.

```diff
diff --git a/src/classes/wrapped.cpp b/src/classes/wrapped.cpp
index c5a8cc9..5650fac 100644
--- a/src/classes/wrapped.cpp
+++ b/src/classes/wrapped.cpp
@@ -105,7 +105,10 @@ std::vector<EngineClassRegistrationCallback> &get_engine_class_registration_call
        return engine_class_registration_callbacks;
 }

+std::mutex _prop_list_mutex;
+
 GDExtensionPropertyInfo *create_c_property_list(const ::godot::List<::godot::PropertyInfo> &plist_cpp, uint32_t *r_size) {
+       std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(_prop_list_mutex);
        GDExtensionPropertyInfo *plist = nullptr;
        // Linked list size can be expensive to get so we cache it
        const uint32_t plist_size = plist_cpp.size();
```

A quick POC that seems to fix the crash in my testes (applied to `godot-cpp` in the extensions).
